From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:35:21 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: dt-bindings: ti,tas27xx: Allow ti,tas2764 as the
 SN012776 fallback

The Apple device trees describe their SN012776 speaker amps as
"ti,sn012776", "ti,tas2764". The driver matches the more specific
ti,sn012776 for the quirks of the Apple variant, and ti,tas2764 names
the part it derives from. The binding allows a single compatible only,
so dt-validate reports the compatible as too long on every amp of those
machines.

Allow ti,sn012776 followed by ti,tas2764. The single compatibles stay
valid.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit c120db0d98d95a9e43ed609beee3cef3b4e5b3df)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas27xx.yaml        | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas27xx.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas27xx.yaml
index f48d3f3750..99eebcfabb 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas27xx.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas27xx.yaml
@@ -27,10 +27,14 @@ allOf:
 
 properties:
   compatible:
-    enum:
-      - ti,tas2764
-      - ti,tas2780
-      - ti,sn012776 # Apple variant of TAS2764
+    oneOf:
+      - enum:
+          - ti,tas2764
+          - ti,tas2780
+          - ti,sn012776 # Apple variant of TAS2764
+      - items:
+          - const: ti,sn012776
+          - const: ti,tas2764
 
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
